   "evidence": "Proof body is `have h2 : (2:\u211d) \u2264 Fintype.card \u03b9 := by exact_mod_cast h; nlinarith` \u2014 nothing about `\u03b9` or `Fintype` enters. Used at lines 189, 198, 231 and 436, each time applied to a hypothesis of the form `1 < Fintype.card \u03b9`, so the \u2115-level statement applies verbatim. Contrast `Finset.sum_sum_erase_const' ... (s : Finset \u03b9)` at EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Algebra/BigOperators/Finset.lean:38-40, which is stated for arbitrary `#s`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Nuclear/Medium/Collective/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Restate as `theorem ... {m : \u2115} (h : 1 < m) : (0:\u211d) < m * (m - 1)` (naturally alongside `sum_sum_erase_const'` in `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Algebra/BigOperators/Finset.lean`, where the same `M (M - 1)` count already lives). The three call sites are unchanged: `card_mul_card_sub_one_pos h` still elaborates with `m := Fintype.card \u03b9` inferred from `h`.",
   "issue": "`card_mul_card_sub_one_pos (h : 1 < Fintype.card \u03b9) : (0:\u211d) < Fintype.card \u03b9 * (Fintype.card \u03b9 - 1)` is a pure arithmetic fact about a natural number cast to \u211d, but is stated only for `Fintype.card \u03b9` under `[Fintype \u03b9]`. It is therefore unusable for `Finset.card`, even though the PR's own pair-counting lemma `Finset.sum_sum_erase_const'` is deliberately stated for an arbitrary `Finset s` with `#s * (#s - 1)` pairs, so the follow-up variance/four-particle work will have to re-prove it.",
